{"nodes": [{"id": "design_money_manager_design_system", "label": "Money Manager Design System", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "DESIGN.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "design_lit_column_of_water", "label": "The Lit Column of Water (north star)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "DESIGN.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The figure and the field are the same fact: safe-to-spend is set over a water surface whose fill height is that figure. Material 3 tonal elevation already treats nearer-the-light as lighter, so the metaphor rides the platform instead of fighting it. There is no backdrop blur anywhere, by decision, because Compose at this version has no backdrop filter and a fake blur would be the dishonest half of the material."}, {"id": "design_depth_ladder", "label": "Five-Step Depth Ladder", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "DESIGN.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Shelf/Trench/Deep/Night/Abyss, index 0 nearest the light, is both the ground gradient and the source of every plate bed, so one ordering governs the whole screen. Light scheme runs the same five steps from white down."}, {"id": "design_glass_plate", "label": "Modifier.glassPlate(shape, depth)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "DESIGN.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "design_elevation_is_depth_rule", "label": "The Elevation Is Depth Rule", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "DESIGN.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A plate's bed alpha and tint are a function of its depth argument and nothing else. Never a drop shadow, never a hand-picked alpha, never a border to fake a lift; there is not one Modifier.shadow in the UI source."}, {"id": "design_transmission_rule", "label": "The Transmission Rule", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "DESIGN.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The gradient and its caustics are drawn once behind everything; a plate that paints itself opaque buries the only reason the ground exists."}, {"id": "design_one_warm_hue_rule", "label": "The One Warm Hue Rule", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "DESIGN.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Sun means goals and streaks and nothing else, and is excluded from categoryScale() on purpose, so a warm mark anywhere in the app means exactly one thing."}, {"id": "design_expenses_are_not_red_rule", "label": "The Expenses Are Not Red Rule", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "DESIGN.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "In a tracker you log expenses all day; painting each one as an alarm makes the alarm meaningless. Expense amounts take Expense Ink and only over-budget and overdue reach for alert."}, {"id": "design_never_colour_alone_rule", "label": "The Never-Colour-Alone Rule", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "DESIGN.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Every amount has a sign and sits in a tabular column, and every over state pairs its tone with a written label, so a screen reader and a colour-blind eye get the same fact."}, {"id": "design_real_money_rule", "label": "The Real Money Rule", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "DESIGN.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A figure the eye lands on or scans down a column is rendered through MoneyText in a MoneyType style; money inside a running sentence uses money() in the sentence's style, because tabular figures exist to align a column and there is no column inside a sentence. Counts, percentages and day numbers are not money. The Glance widget is the one exception, and not by choice: it has no access to the app's font."}, {"id": "design_cents_are_shown_rule", "label": "The Cents Are Shown Rule", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "DESIGN.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Money is Long minor units formatted by moneyParts; cents are always present and never emphasised (64% size, 52% alpha). Never Double, never rounded away."}, {"id": "design_no_eyebrow_rule", "label": "The No Eyebrow Rule", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "DESIGN.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A section heading carries its own weight: title, optional caption, optional trailing text action. No kicker, no numbering, no all-caps label stacked above a heading."}, {"id": "design_screen_pays_its_own_status_bar_rule", "label": "The Screen Pays Its Own Status Bar Rule", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "DESIGN.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The shell's Scaffold deliberately omits the top inset so the Home hero can run under the status bar; each screen re-applies it in exactly one place (TabColumn insetTop, DetailScaffold's app bar insets, the lock screen's windowInsetsPadding). Handing the top inset back to the shell is what put the hero in a box in the first place."}, {"id": "design_one_authored_motion_rule", "label": "The One Authored Motion Rule", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "DESIGN.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The app has one authored gesture and it is filling; every other animated surface is a quieter instance of the same gesture, so there is no second hero motion in a different idiom. Every animated surface reads motionEnabled() first and collapses to a zero-duration tween when Remove animations is on."}, {"id": "design_arriving_curve_rule", "label": "The Arriving Curve Rule", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "DESIGN.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Material's FastOutSlowInEasing belongs to something travelling between two on-screen positions; it accelerates in, and nothing arriving should accelerate in. Reaching for the familiar standard curve already put the wrong easing on every entrance in this app once."}, {"id": "design_reveal_plays_once_rule", "label": "The Reveal Plays Once Rule", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "DESIGN.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A LazyColumn disposes an item when it scrolls out, so a bare animateFloatAsState replays the reveal on every scroll back and the gesture becomes a loop the user triggers by scrolling. rememberFill keeps its played flag in rememberSaveable and comes back already full."}, {"id": "design_photography_rule", "label": "The Photography Rule", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "DESIGN.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Photographs appear in exactly one place, a savings goal, where a picture of the thing being saved for does real work. A picture that is not the user's own content is not content: no stock imagery in empty states, no decorative texture, no illustrated onboarding."}, {"id": "design_feedback_is_not_a_gesture_rule", "label": "The Feedback Is Not A Gesture Rule", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "DESIGN.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Material's own feedback grammar (press state, spring settle on a keypress, haptic at commit) is not a second authored motion and needs no justification against the filling gesture; what it must never do is animate something not responding to a user action in that moment."}, {"id": "design_real_fab_rule", "label": "The Real FAB Rule", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "DESIGN.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "One floating action per screen, and only where the primary action exists. A FAB that does nothing is worse than no FAB, and a circular add button inside the navigation bar is an iOS tab-bar habit."}, {"id": "design_water_column", "label": "Signature: The Water Column", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "DESIGN.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A vertical scrim holds type contrast at any fill level, so the world's own light falloff does the accessibility work rather than a plate behind the text. over = true inverts the reading and turns the fill to alert, always paired with a sign and a written label."}, {"id": "design_submerged_photograph", "label": "Signature: The Submerged Photograph", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "DESIGN.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "SubmergedPhoto draws the same two-sine swell over a goal's picture at 62% tint so the image reads through the water instead of being painted out, and the level is the goal's own fraction, so the thing you are saving for goes under as you save."}, {"id": "design_merchant_monogram", "label": "Merchant Monogram", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "DESIGN.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The disc tint is a function of the merchant's own name hashed into categoryScale(), so one merchant keeps one colour forever and a column of rows stops looking like a column of the same row; the category survives as a small badge."}, {"id": "design_hand_drawn_charts", "label": "Signature: Hand-drawn Charts", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "DESIGN.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Ring labels ride their own arc as real text nodes instead of sitting in a legend, so TalkBack reads the ring as a list. No chart library: a kit brings its own gridlines and categorical rainbow into a committed world, and theming arguments never get them back out."}, {"id": "design_category_scale", "label": "categoryScale() (eight-step cool scale)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "DESIGN.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "design_moneytext", "label": "MoneyText", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "DESIGN.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "design_money_parts", "label": "moneyParts (Long minor units)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "DESIGN.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "design_bleed_modifier", "label": "Modifier.bleed()", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "DESIGN.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The single sanctioned escape from the 20dp gutter, used only when an item is the screen's thesis: a thesis about a column of water cannot be delivered inside a card inset on four sides."}, {"id": "design_money_motion", "label": "MoneyMotion (duration and easing tokens)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "DESIGN.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "design_motion_enabled", "label": "motionEnabled()", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "DESIGN.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "design_remember_fill", "label": "rememberFill", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "DESIGN.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "design_archivo_type_scale", "label": "Archivo Variable Type Scale", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "DESIGN.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Archivo run wide (wdth 112-118) gives figures a broad engineered stance; the same family at wdth 100 keeps headings in the family without competing with the money. Width is earned: wide means the number is real money."}, {"id": "design_responsive_breakpoint", "label": "640dp Breakpoint (bar vs rail)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "DESIGN.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Below 640dp a five-item bottom bar, at or above it a leading navigation rail, never a stretched phone bar. The water ground drifts only on Home and Lock, because a background that animates on every screen is a battery bill, not a design."}, {"id": "design_dynamic_color_opt_in", "label": "Dynamic Color Off By Default", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "DESIGN.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A wallpaper-derived scheme reorders the depth ladder until the waterline stops meaning anything, so it is opt-in in Appearance."}, {"id": "design_no_dead_controls", "label": "No Control Wired To Nothing", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "DESIGN.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Either a control acts, or it is disabled with a stated reason, or it is not drawn; a button that absorbs a tap in silence is the one defect a user cannot diagnose. The condition that would refuse a tap belongs in enabled, never in an early return inside onClick."}, {"id": "design_gutter_and_rhythm", "label": "20dp Gutter and Spacing Rhythm", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "DESIGN.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}], "edges": [{"source": "design_money_manager_design_system", "target": "design_lit_column_of_water", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "DESIGN.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "design_money_manager_design_system", "target": "design_water_column", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "DESIGN.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "design_money_manager_design_system", "target": "design_submerged_photograph", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "DESIGN.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "design_money_manager_design_system", "target": "design_hand_drawn_charts", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "DESIGN.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "design_money_manager_design_system", "target": "design_merchant_monogram", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "DESIGN.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "design_money_manager_design_system", "target": "design_gutter_and_rhythm", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "DESIGN.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "design_money_manager_design_system", "target": "design_archivo_type_scale", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "DESIGN.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "design_money_manager_design_system", "target": "design_depth_ladder", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "DESIGN.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "design_money_manager_design_system", "target": "product_binding_visual_constraint", "relation": "references", "confidence": "INFERRED", "confidence_score": 0.85, "source_file": "DESIGN.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "design_lit_column_of_water", "target": "design_depth_ladder", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "DESIGN.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "design_lit_column_of_water", "target": "design_water_column", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "DESIGN.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "design_lit_column_of_water", "target": "design_transmission_rule", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "DESIGN.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "design_depth_ladder", "target": "design_glass_plate", "relation": "shares_data_with", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "DESIGN.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "design_elevation_is_depth_rule", "target": "design_glass_plate", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "DESIGN.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "design_transmission_rule", "target": "design_glass_plate", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "DESIGN.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "design_one_warm_hue_rule", "target": "design_category_scale", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "DESIGN.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "design_one_warm_hue_rule", "target": "readme_goals_and_savings", "relation": "references", "confidence": "INFERRED", "confidence_score": 0.85, "source_file": "DESIGN.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "design_merchant_monogram", "target": "design_category_scale", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "DESIGN.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "design_hand_drawn_charts", "target": "design_category_scale", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "DESIGN.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "design_hand_drawn_charts", "target": "readme_reports_and_insights", "relation": "references", "confidence": "INFERRED", "confidence_score": 0.95, "source_file": "DESIGN.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "design_expenses_are_not_red_rule", "target": "design_never_colour_alone_rule", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "INFERRED", "confidence_score": 0.85, "source_file": "DESIGN.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "design_never_colour_alone_rule", "target": "product_accessibility_commitments", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "INFERRED", "confidence_score": 0.95, "source_file": "DESIGN.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "design_real_money_rule", "target": "design_moneytext", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "DESIGN.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source